  "extractionNotes": "Stillbirth where the sex could not be determined, so no registry act was drawn up; proof is the special doctor/midwife stillbirth certificate. The grant is evidenced by the ZUS account screen (benefit title 1240 from 2025-09-20 to 2025-11-14, 56 days; maternity benefit row from 2025-09-20) and a case-closure note saying the case ended with payment. No decision; rate not printed (100% expected for the 8-week leave). The leave application asks for 8 weeks from the birth but writes the end date one day too late (57 days by its dates); the plan uses the 8 weeks (56 days) the application names. The account screen also shows two days of unpaid leave immediately before the birth (2025-09-18..19); there is no field for an unpaid-leave break and it did not affect the grant. Z-3 salary table 2024-09..2025-08 (12 months before the birth); column 6 is the contractual amount and contributionBase is inferred equal to it; 2025-02 had sickness days. Employer marked up to 20 insured. Working-time fraction not legible. asOf = date of the leave application and the stillbirth certificate (the ZUS screen and closure note are undated)."
